<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">French Protectorate of Madagascar</h1><p class="st-meta">1885 CE – 1897 CE · capital Antananarivo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The French protectorate imposed on the Merina monarchy of Madagascar, a step between independence and outright colonial conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/merina-kingdom">Merina Kingdom</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-hova-war">Franco-Hova War</a> of 1883-1885. The treaty of December 1885 gave France control over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar's</a> foreign relations, the bay of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/diego-suarez-colony">Diego-Suarez</a> and a resident-general at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antananarivo">Antananarivo</a>, though the Merina government kept internal power.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranavalona-iii">Queen Ranavalona III</a> and her prime minister and husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rainilaiarivony">Rainilaiarivony</a> continued to govern through a modernised administration, a Protestant state church and an army. They disputed French claims to a full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> recognised French rights only in 1890. Debts from the war indemnity weakened the monarchy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1895 a French expedition marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antananarivo">Antananarivo</a>, which fell in September. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menalamba-rebellion">Menalamba rising</a> followed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed the island in 1896. In February 1897 General Gallieni abolished the monarchy and exiled the queen, making the island the colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-madagascar">French Madagascar</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="protectorate, 1885 CE – 1897 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">protectorate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.21%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1885 CE – 1897 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Antananarivo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ranavalona III, Rainilaiarivony</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestant Christianity, Malagasy traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malagasy, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Protectorate of Madagascar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1891&amp;focus=french-protectorate-of-madagascar" aria-label="French Protectorate of Madagascar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5966 2878 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French Protectorate of Madagascar lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6286 3134L6286 3134M6286 3134L5054 728M6286 3134L6286 3134"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6286 3134h0M5054 728h0M6286 3134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6286 3134h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6286 3134h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Antananarivo. <a href="/atlas?year=1891&amp;focus=french-protectorate-of-madagascar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
